# Understanding Intelligent Contracts on GenLayer

## Why Traditional Smart Contracts Are Limited

Traditional smart contracts were designed around deterministic execution.

Given the same input, every validator must always produce the exact same output.

This works extremely well for:
- payments
- token transfers
- strict rule-based logic

However, AI-native applications introduce a completely different challenge.

AI systems operate through:
- reasoning
- probabilities
- interpretation
- contextual understanding

These systems are not purely deterministic.

## What Makes GenLayer Different

GenLayer introduces Intelligent Contracts.

Instead of relying purely on rigid deterministic execution, Intelligent Contracts support reasoning-oriented workflows and AI-native applications.

According to GenLayer documentation, Intelligent Contracts can:
- process natural language
- access web data
- evaluate unstructured information
- support non-deterministic operations

This creates a new design space for decentralized systems.

